# Files that are executed inside Linux containers must keep LF endings on every
# platform. With `core.autocrlf=true` (the common Windows default) a checkout
# would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF, and bash then fails on the first line:
#
#   /scripts/migrate.sh: line 12: $'\r': command not found
#   /scripts/migrate.sh: line 13: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# scripts/ and db/ are bind-mounted straight into the migrate container by
# infra/docker/compose.yml, so they are affected even without a rebuild.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
